  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef has decided that he will cut down on his calorie intake. He will eat atmost XXX calories in a day.\n\nToday, he already ate YYY sweets, each having ZZZ calories. Find out how many more calories he can eat. If he has already exceeded his limit, output −1-1−1.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains 333 integers - X,YX, YX,Y and ZZZ.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line\n\n\n\n−1-1−1 if Chef has exceeded his calorie limit\nThe amount of calories Chef can still eat if he has not exceeded it",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X,Y,Z≤1001 \\le X, Y, Z \\le 1001≤X,Y,Z≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 2 4",
        "output": "2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef was allowed to eat 888 calories. He already ate 2⋅4=82 \\cdot 4 = 82⋅4=8. Therefore, he has 10−8=210 - 8 = 210−8=2 calories more till he hits his limit."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "10 2 6",
        "output": "-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nChef was allowed to eat 888 calories, but he already ate 2⋅6=122 \\cdot 6 = 122⋅6=12. Therefore, he has exceeded his limit already, and we print −1-1−1."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100 10 10",
        "output": "0",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
